// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-collapse.py --gopp %gopp --out %t | FileCheck %s
// P03.25 (GEN-14, UNI-5, R7 to R9, owner decision 2026-10-30): generic code
// whose units cancel at an instance computes what plain code does, so no
// instance is an error. The collapse sites are recorded (`unit-site`) and the
// unit parameters whose units the code needs at run time (`unit-dict`) are
// passed on by the GEN-12 use fixpoint, with no cap: a chain of 40 and of 200
// generics written callers first (every one needs the units of the leaf's
// `a / b`), a leaf with 4500 distinct unit types behind a caller, and a
// generic of the main package that forwards to a second package, which calls
// a generic of a third. Each shape with units that cancel with the factor 1000
// and with units that agree, checked with 1 and 8 body threads (the same
// errors and the same dump).
// CHECK: chain40 cancel                     errors=0 dicts=40 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: chain40 agree                      errors=0 dicts=40 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: chain200 cancel                    errors=0 dicts=200 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: chain200 agree                     errors=0 dicts=200 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: uses4500 cancel                    errors=0 dicts=2 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: uses4500 agree                     errors=0 dicts=2 sites=1 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: forwarder-package cancel           errors=0 dicts=1 sites=0 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NEXT: forwarder-package agree            errors=0 dicts=1 sites=0 j1==j8:yes ok
// CHECK-NOT: FAIL
